.TH IP-AUDIT-SUBSCRIBER 1 "November 2026" "Kea IP Audit Hook" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ip-audit-subscriber \- search lease events by subscriber identifier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ip-audit-subscriber
.B --type
.I IDENTIFIER_TYPE
.B --value
.I VALUE
.B --from
.I TIMESTAMP
.B --to
.I TIMESTAMP
.I LOGS
[
.I LOGS
...]
[
.B --json
|
.B --table
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ip-audit-subscriber
searches a timezone-aware time range for exact, case-sensitive matches in the selected
subscriber identifier field. Matching events are shown across the subscriber's IP
addresses, with reconstructed lease interval context and source-file locations.
.PP
The range is half-open: events at
.I --from
are included and events at
.I --to
are excluded. A base log path includes that file and numbered rotations, including gzip
rotations. Explicit files and quoted shell glob patterns are also accepted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --type " IDENTIFIER_TYPE"
Required record field: circuit-id, remote-id, subscriber-id, hw-address, client-id, or duid.
.TP
.BI --value " VALUE"
Required exact value in the representation present in the log. Matching is case-sensitive.
.TP
.BI --from " TIMESTAMP"
Required inclusive ISO 8601 start timestamp with a timezone.
.TP
.BI --to " TIMESTAMP"
Required exclusive ISO 8601 end timestamp with a timezone, later than the start.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B --json
Write identifier and range metadata and matching events, including each full source record.
.TP
.B --table
Write stable tab-separated columns with a header row.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I LOGS
One or more log files, base log paths, or quoted glob patterns. A base path includes
that file and its numbered or gzip-compressed rotations.
.SH OUTPUT
Readable text is the default. Table columns include timestamp, event, IP address, lease
start/end, address family, lease type, server, and source file/line. JSON includes the
complete matching source records. Exit status is 0 when matches exist, 1 when no events
match, and 2 for invalid input or unreadable or malformed logs.
.SH PRIVACY AND LIMITATIONS
Identifiers and JSON records are sensitive subscriber data. Restrict access to the command
and protect redirected output like the audit logs. Results are inferred from available logs,
not queried from Kea's live database. Missing events or custom field selections can omit
matches or interval context. Full logs are loaded into memory; use relevant log files and
one allocation domain at a time.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
ip-audit-subscriber --type circuit-id --value 706f72742d372f33 \\
  --from 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z --to 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z \\
  /var/log/kea/ip-audit.log
ip-audit-subscriber --type hw-address --value aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff \\
  --from 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z --to 2026-11-02T00:00:00Z \\
  --json /var/log/kea/ip-audit.log
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip-audit-lookup (1),
.BR ip-audit-list (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Kea IP Audit Hook contributors.